  {
    "description": "Show the user a report: a document that opens on their screen and stays in their reports. Use it only when the user asks for a report, document or write-up, or when the result is long and worth keeping (in-depth research, a multi-day itinerary, a draft). Never use it to sum up work you did: say the outcome instead. Write well-structured markdown (headings, short paragraphs, lists, tables, links), add blocks for options, comparisons, numbers and itineraries, or build it from blocks alone. Afterwards, say a one-line takeaway. To revise a report you showed earlier, pass its id.",
