  {
    "description": "Search what you and the user said earlier in the conversation, before it was summarised, and the reports you made. Use it when they refer to something from before, or the summary lacks a detail, before asking them to repeat it. With query: the best matching moments. With around (a ref from a result): the conversation just before and after that moment. Results are history, not new requests.",
    "name": "recall",
    "parameters": {
      "properties": {
        "after": {
          "description": "YYYY-MM-DD: only from this day on, when the user names a time",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "around": {
          "description": "A ref from an earlier result, like item:1234, to see the conversation around it",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "before": {
          "description": "YYYY-MM-DD: only before this day",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "done": {
          "description": "The same step in past tense, e.g. \"Opened the library website\".",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "query": {
          "description": "Words to find, e.g. hotel Lisbon. All words must match; put OR between alternatives (hotel OR apartment), quotes around an exact phrase, and * after the start of a word",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "status": {
          "description": "Short user-facing step label, present progressive, e.g. \"Opening the library website\".",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "status"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "type": "function"
  },
  {
    "description": "Create a schedule: recurring (cron, in the user's timezone) or once at a time. When it fires, its prompt arrives in this conversation as a scheduled message for you to act on. Use for reminders, daily briefings and monitoring (\"check X and tell me if Y\"). Write the prompt as a self-contained instruction to yourself.",
    "name": "schedule_create",
